      "title": "Anchor a New Acquaintance's Name to an Outstanding Feature",
      "description": "Human brains register faces intuitively while treating abstract names like meaningless noise. Coupling a substitute word to a salient facial feature forces cognitive registration at the moment of introduction.",
      "category": "daily-routine",
