      "category": "Psychology",
      "type": "mental-model",
      "headline": "Original Awareness Precedes Memory",
      "body": "You cannot forget something you never actually learned. When you misplace your glasses, you did not suffer memory loss; you suffered inattention. True memory begins the microsecond you deliberately observe what you are doing.",
